quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  19,77,Have you seen the one who rejects Our revelations and says: ‘I shall certainly be granted (plenty of) wealth and children’?
  19,78,Has he come to know the Unseen or received a pledge from the Most-Compassionate (Lord)?
  19,79,"No, indeed! We shall record what he says and keep prolonging his punishment (endlessly)."
  19,80,"We shall take over from him what he claims, and he will come to Us alone (without wealth and children)."
  19,81,They have taken gods besides Allah so that they may be (a source of) strength and honour for them.
  19,82,"No, indeed! They (i.e. the false gods) shall soon disown their worship, and they will become their opponents."
  19,83,Do you not realise that We sent the devils upon the disbelievers? They keep inciting them cunningly (to commit wrongs).
  19,84,So be not in haste towards them (for their punishment). We are just counting down their days.
  19,85,"On the Day, We will gather the God-conscious towards the Most-Compassionate (Lord) as an honoured delegation."
  19,86,And We will drive the guilty as a thirsty herd towards Hell.
  19,87,"(On that Day,) none will possess the (power of) intercession except the one who has (already) taken a promise from the Most-Compassionate (Lord)."
  19,88,They say: ‘The Most-Compassionate (Lord) has taken a child!’
  19,89,You have indeed asserted a terrible thing!
  19,90,"The heavens can almost burst apart at it, the earth can split asunder, and the mountains can crumble to pieces,"
  19,91,(protesting) that they attribute a son to the Most-Compassionate (Lord)!
  19,92,It is not befitting for (the Glory of) the Most-Compassionate (Lord) to take a child.
  19,93,There is none in the heavens and the earth but will come to the Most-Compassionate (Lord) as a servant.
  19,94,"Indeed, He has (accurately) counted them (all) and numbered them precisely."
  19,95,"And each of them shall come to Him on the Day of Resurrection, all alone."
